<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32024" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏbustus</span></b> , a, um,
			Part. [ob-uro]. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>burnt around</i>, <i>burnt</i>, <i>hardened in the
			fire</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hic torre armatus obusto,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 7, 506</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sudes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 11, 894</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">glaeba gelu,</span>”
				<i>burnt by frost</i>.
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 5, 2, 66</span></i>
			. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
